Checking traps by hand means a click, a walk, and a panel for each trap. Trapline does it in one click and shows all your traps in a compact grid. Walks, action times, and rewards stay the same as by hand.

Fun fact: a [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trapline]trapline[/url] is a route a trapper follows to set and check traps. Now your character has one too.

[size=5]Main features[/size]
[list]
[*][b]Take All.[/b] One click collects every trap with prey, also Auto Trap Cages, along the shortest walk: your floor first, then the next one by the stairs.[/*]
[*][b]Trap grid.[/b] Your traps and free Trap Slots by floor and zone. Gold marks prey, and red marks a trap that breaks at its next pickup. Point at a cell for the game's trap card, and pin the list to keep it open.[/*]
[*][b]Set and replace traps.[/b] Click + on a free slot to set a trap from your backpack or home storage. Auto-replace (on by default) sets a new trap of the same kind when one breaks.[/*]
[/list]

Trapline does not rebait traps. The Auto-replace settings are small values in your save, which the game ignores if you remove the mod.

[size=5]Compatibility[/size]
[b]Not compatible:[/b]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/6]TrapPickAll[/url]: it replaces the game's trap pickup with its own, and Trapline queues the game's normal pickup. Use one of the two.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5]Requirements[/size]
[list]
[*]Survival Log 1.1.18599 or later.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx for Survival Log[/url]. Install it first.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5]Installation[/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx[/url] [i](if no other mods were installed before, start the game once so BepInEx finishes setup, then quit)[/i].[/*]
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path example:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Survival Log\BepInEx\plugins\Trapline.dll[/code][/*][/list]

[size=5]Uninstall[/size]
Delete [font=Courier New]Trapline.dll[/font] from the [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font] folder.

